  "key_pattern": "^(?=\\d{12}$)996(?:31[25]|3\\d{3})",
  "usage": "nine-digit number without the leading 0: 312 123456, +996 3222 12345 or (3922) 5-12-34. Written inside the country a number starts with the trunk 0 (0312 …, 03922 …): drop that 0. Type the whole number: a code on its own does not match, so that it can't collide with other countries' codes",
  "note": "Nine-digit national numbers; Bishkek has the three-digit code 312, other places four-digit codes: 31xx Chüy, 32xx Osh Region (3222 Osh city), 34xx Talas, 35xx Naryn, 36xx Batken, 37xx Jalal-Abad, 39xx Issyk-Kul. The 316x, 326x, 346x, 356x, 366x, 376x–377x and 396x codes are KyrgyzTelecom's CDMA-450 fixed-wireless numbers for the same towns.",
  "miss_note": "not a geographic Kyrgyz landline: a number written with the trunk 0 (drop the 0 and look it up again), a mobile number (20X, 22X, 50X, 51X, 54X–57X, 70X, 77X, 99X), 52X (satellite), 6XX (fixed numbers without a place), 800 (freephone), or a number of another country",
  "source": [
